.TH JANK 1 "2026-11-05" "jank 0.1~git20261101.f3d82d6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jank \- native Clojure dialect on LLVM with C++ interop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jank
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jank
evaluates and compiles jank, Clojure and C++ sources. It provides a REPL and a JIT
for interactive development and compiles programs ahead of time to native code.
jank is alpha quality software.
.PP
Run
.B jank help
for the complete list of options of the installed version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fIfile\fR
Load and run a file.
.TP
.B repl
Start a terminal REPL client and an nREPL server.
.TP
.B cpp-repl
Start a terminal C++ REPL client.
.TP
.B run-main \fImodule\fR
Load a module and execute its \-main function.
.TP
.B compile-module \fImodule\fR
Compile a module (given its namespace) and its dependencies ahead of time.
.TP
.B compile \fImodule\fR
Compile a project ahead of time, with an entry point module containing \-main.
.TP
.B check-health
Report on the state of the jank installation: its resource directory, the Clang it
uses, and whether JIT and AOT compilation work.
.TP
.B print-binary-version
Print the current binary version and exit.
.TP
.B print-cflags
Print the Clang flags for AOT compilation of C++ source code and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print the help message and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-module\-path \fIpath\fR
A colon separated list of directories, JAR files and ZIP files to search for modules.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
The port the nREPL server binds to; 0 or omitted selects a random free port.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-optimization " \fI0\-3\fR"
The optimization level for AOT compilation.
.TP
.B \-\-runtime \fIstatic\fR|\fIdynamic\fR
The AOT runtime to target (default: static).
.TP
.B \-\-target\-dir \fIpath\fR
The directory for final artifacts (default: target).
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-include\-dir " \fIpath\fR"
A directory for include resolution; may be given several times.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-define\-macro " \fIname\fR[=\fIvalue\fR]"
Define a preprocessor macro; may be given several times.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-library\-dir " \fIpath\fR"
A directory to search for libraries; may be given several times.
.TP
.B \-l\fIlib\fR
Link a library; may be given several times.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/jank/0.1
jank's resource directory: headers, runtime libraries and core library sources.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/jank
Per-user cache, including the precompiled header jank builds on first use.
.SH NOTES
jank uses clang++\-22 at runtime for its JIT and for AOT compilation. Its sources are
UTF\-8; run it in a UTF\-8 locale.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clang (1)
.PP
The jank book: https://book.jank-lang.org/
